# Local bash assignments, loaded quietly by the native commands.
# Obtain secrets from this machine's own secret store, never from a chat.
# Keep maestro.env private (0600); setup.sh preserves an existing file.
# Quote values with shell metacharacters; keep this file to assignments.

#MAESTRO_PORT=8001
#OPENAI_API_KEY=''
#GEMINI_API_KEY=''
#OPENAI_BASE_URL=''
#FAST_MODEL=''
#SMART_MODEL=''
#CHAT_MODEL=''

# Always-on copy only: the laptop's address. No path and no query.
# A tunnel on this machine: http://127.0.0.1:8101
# HTTPS through Funnel: https://<mac>.<tailnet>.ts.net (docs/sync-setup.md).
# If a proxy decrypts TLS, set these here. A cron restart has no shell environment.
#HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example:3128
#NO_PROXY=127.0.0.1,localhost
#SSL_CERT_FILE=
# Sync is on when $MAESTRO_HOME/sync-key exists; never put the key itself in this file.
#SYNC_REMOTE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8101

# The commands enforce local data paths, loopback hosts, one worker,
# MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2, EMBEDDINGS_OUT_OF_PROCESS=1, and a disk model cache.
